"""Packet transcripts recorded from pion/sctp v1.12.0.

Two pion associations talked over an in-memory datagram pipe while every
packet was logged in wire order. "A" is a default pion client, as
pion/webrtc creates it. "B" is a pion association with I-DATA support
switched off, which is what A sees when it talks to this library.

Each line is `<who> <milliseconds> <hex packet>`. `A!` marks a packet the
recorder dropped on purpose, and `#` lines are notes: what the application
on side B received, and which scripted step begins.

The script: handshake; a 31-byte ordered DCEP OPEN (PPID 50) on stream 0,
answered by B with a 4-byte ACK; a 3000-byte message (PPID 53) in three
fragments; a DCEP OPEN on stream 2 and an unordered, max-retransmits-0
message on it; two small ordered messages back to back; a stream reset of
stream 2 from both sides; an ABORT.
"""


def pion_cs() -> List[String]:
    """A is the client and B the server: A alone sends INIT."""
    var lines = List[String]()
    lines.append("A 0 13881388000000006e3f86130100001c6521be7000100000ffffffffc7c844f38008000882c040c2")
    lines.append("B 0 138813886521be700f9a40a30200003e817b583500100000ffffffffd8d60a0b000700247374f5a3f9756885d2ea036bca4d68f93921bc88a4a35753d76fa93d3ba2705d8008000682c00000")
